  "lineage": "Grew from ethnographic cylinder collecting around 1890 into an autonomous listening practice after R. Murray Schafer's World Soundscape Project in Vancouver in the early 1970s, extended by Chris Watson, Annea Lockwood, Hildegard Westerkamp and Francisco Lopez — unaccompanied environmental sound captured with stereo or hydrophone arrays to portable recorders, presented with minimal edit, no metre and no pitch centre, structured only by the duration and dynamics of the place itself.",
